.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_MEM_MGMT_PROCS 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs \- set custom memory management for the allocations of the async engine of chttpclient
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Every chttpcli instance in this process shares one ccol_event_loop
reactor for its Tier 2 and Tier 3 work. This function sends every
allocation of that reactor to the malloc, free, calloc and realloc in
mp. Those allocations hold the registration table, the dispatch state
of each connection, the worker pool for DNS and for connect, and more.
This works in the same way as the memory management procs of every
other module in this library. An mp of NULL puts the default allocator
back.

Each chttpcli instance also has an allocator for its own requests and
connections. You set that allocator with ccol_create_chttpclient_mp,
which follows the usual _mp convention. This function is independent
of it. It affects only the construction of the one shared reactor.

You can call this function only at two times. The first time is before
the reactor ever starts in this process. That is before the first call
to chttpclient_do_async or to chttpclient_do_async_streaming anywhere.
The second time is after the engine stops completely. The engine stops
after every async user of a chttpcli drops its reference and the
automatic teardown finishes. The reactor of
chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs usually lives for the whole
process. This engine is different, because it starts and stops on its
own with the Tier 2 and Tier 3 traffic. The window for this call
therefore comes back again and again. It is not one chance at the
start of the process.

If mp is not NULL, all four function pointers in it must be set. Those
pointers are malloc, free, calloc and realloc.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, if the call succeeds.
ccol_invalid_args, if mp is not NULL but holds a function pointer that
    is NULL.
ccol_not_permitted, while the engine runs. Wait for the engine to stop
    completely first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3)
